Two parts, both before merge. (a) Mustafa turns on GitHub secret scanning and push protection: Settings > Code security, both free for public repositories. (b) In checkpoint.mjs save(), between the `git diff --cached --quiet` check and the commit, add:
const SECRET = /gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}|github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}|sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}|AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----|xox[abpr]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}|:\/\/[^\s\/:@]+:[^\s\/@]+@/;
for (const f of git('diff', '--cached', '--name-only', '--diff-filter=AM', '--', DIR).out.split('\n').filter(Boolean)) {
  const t = git('show', `:${f}`);
  if (!t.ok || SECRET.test(t.out)) { git('reset', '-q', '--', DIR); log(`refused: ${f} looks like a secret or is over 1 MB; nothing committed`); return 2; }
}
Add one test: a notes file holding a fake ghp_ token gives exit 2, and the remote stays unchanged. A failed `git show` covers execFileSync's 1 MB maxBuffer, so oversized files are refused too.

